# Planora AI — Architecture Specification

This document outlines the architectural patterns, database schemas, state transitions, and security boundaries implemented in Planora AI.

---

## 1. System Topology

```mermaid
graph TD
    Client[Client Browser / SPA] -->|HTTPS| VercelEdge[Vercel Edge Network]
    VercelEdge -->|Static Assets| Frontend[React 19 SPA]
    VercelEdge -->|/api/v1/*| ServerlessGateway[FastAPI Serverless Function]

    subgraph Middleware Pipeline
        ServerlessGateway --> RateLimiter[Sliding Window Rate Limiter]
        RateLimiter --> PayloadGuard[2MB Payload Limiter]
        PayloadGuard --> SecurityHeaders[Security Headers Middleware]
    end

    subgraph Service Layer
        SecurityHeaders --> AuthRouter[Auth Router]
        SecurityHeaders --> PlansRouter[Plans Router]

        AuthRouter --> SessionService[Session & User Service]
        PlansRouter --> PlanService[Plan Orchestration Service]

        SessionService --> Database[(Neon PostgreSQL)]
        PlanService --> Database
    end

    subgraph AI Engine
        PlanService --> AIPlannerInterface[AI Planner Interface]
        AIPlannerInterface -->|Primary Provider| GeminiAdapter[Gemini 2.5 Flash Adapter]
        AIPlannerInterface -->|Fallback Provider| MockAdapter[Deterministic Mock Adapter]
    end
```

## 2. Database Schema

### Entity Relationship Diagram

```mermaid
erDiagram
    USERS ||--o{ SESSIONS : "establishes"
    USERS ||--o{ PLANS : "creates"

    USERS {
        uuid id PK
        string email UK
        string password_hash
        string full_name
        boolean is_active
        timestamp created_at
        timestamp updated_at
    }

    SESSIONS {
        uuid id PK
        uuid user_id FK
        string token_hash UK
        string ip_address
        string user_agent
        timestamp expires_at
        timestamp created_at
        timestamp updated_at
    }

    PLANS {
        uuid id PK
        uuid user_id FK
        string title
        string event_type
        date event_date
        string location
        int guest_count
        numeric budget_amount
        string budget_currency
        jsonb priorities
        string style
        string status
        jsonb plan_data
        jsonb generation_metadata
        timestamp created_at
        timestamp updated_at
    }
```

### Sequence Diagram: In-Place Section Regeneration

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Host as Event Host
    participant UI as React UI (PlanDisplay)
    participant API as FastAPI Gateway
    participant DB as Neon PostgreSQL
    participant AI as Gemini 2.5 Flash

    Host->>UI: Triggers section regeneration with refinement notes
    UI->>API: POST /api/v1/plans/{id}/regenerate/{section}
    API->>DB: Query plan record and verify user ownership
    alt Ownership Failure or Missing Record
        API-->>UI: HTTP 404 Not Found (Anti-Enumeration)
    else Verification Success
        API->>AI: Generate isolated section with contextual brief
        AI-->>API: Validated section JSON payload
        API->>DB: Update target section within plan_data JSONB (commit)
        API-->>UI: HTTP 200 with updated PlanResponse
        UI->>Host: Render updated section; preserve manual edits in other sections
    end
```